  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important uncertainty is the performance floor of each modality, which is needed before evaluating whether fusion or more complex encoders add value. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible RNA baseline: no aggregation, no fusion, a standard linear encoder. It establishes the RNA-only reference accuracy against which all subsequent RNA encoder choices (scvi, scgpt), profile settings (multiprofile), and multimodal fusion experiments can be compared. Starting with the simplest configuration avoids confounding multiple design changes and gives a clean anchor point for the 9 remaining experiments."
}

